# Protected branches

Never create commits on `development` or `main`.

- Create or check out a feature/docs/fix branch first, then commit there.
- If a commit lands on `development` or `main` by mistake, move it to a topic
  branch and reset the protected branch to match its remote (only when the
  mistaken commit is local and unpushed).
- Pull requests target `development` (integration) or `main` (release) — do not
  push commits straight onto those branches unless the user explicitly overrides
  this rule for a specific action.
